d_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Medium and Dimensions","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_medium_dims"}],"content":"Watercolor on paper, 11 15/16 x 8 15/16 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Copyright","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_copyright"}],"content":"© Georgia O'Keeffe Museum","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Holding Institution","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_instituion"}],"content":"Metropolitan Museum of Art (The Met)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"The right side of the composition features the red and pink form of a seated, nude woman with pinned-up dark brown hair. Her form contrasts with a bright blue background. The work is loosely painted and has few details.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Artist(s)","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_artist"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Title and Date","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_title_date"}],"content":"Seated Nude, XI, 1917","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"provenance_narrative","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/provenance_narrative"}],"content":"The artist (1917–at least 1966; to Robert Miller); [Robert Miller Gallery, Inc., New York, until 1981; sold to MMA] (Source: The Met, 2025)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Measurement Description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/measurement_description"}],"content":"11 15/16 x 8 15/16 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"cr_remarks_1999","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/cr_remarks_1999"}],"content":["Not recorded Whitney Archive. See cat. no. 176. (Source: Lynes, 1999)"],"type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"selected_references","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/selected_references"}],"content":"Lisa M. Messinger. \"Twentieth Century Art.\" The Metropolitan Museum of Art: Notable Acquisitions, 1981–1982. New York, [1982], p. 62, ill. \n \nLisa Mintz Messinger. \"Georgia O'Keeffe.\" Metropolitan Museum of Art Bulletin 42 (Fall 1984), p. 11, fig. 11 (color). \n \nPhilippe de Montebello. \"[Director's Note].\" Metropolitan Museum of Art Bulletin 42 (Fall 1984), p. 2. \n \nBarbara Haskell. Georgia O'Keeffe: Works on Paper. Exh. cat., Museum of Fine Arts, Museum of New Mexico. Sante Fe, 1985, pp. 3, 100, colorpl. 15. \n \nBenita Eisler. O'Keeffe and Stieglitz: An American Romance. New York, 1991, p. 178. \n \nElizabeth Montgomery. Georgia O'Keeffe. New York, 1993, ill. p. 76 (color). \n \nBarbara Buhler Lynes. Georgia O'Keeffe: Catalogue Raisonné. New Haven, Conn., 1999, vol. 1, p. 107, no. 179, ill. (color). \n \nLisa Mintz Messinger. Georgia O'Keeffe. London, 2001, p. 37, fig. 19 (color). \n \nBarbara Buhler Lynes with Russell Bowman. O'Keeffe's O'Keeffes: The Artist's Collection. Exh. cat., Milwaukee Art Museum. New York, 2001, p. 165, list it with all works included in Exh. Fort Worth and tour 1966. \n \nSamantha Friedman. Georgia O'Keeffe: To See Takes Time. Exh. cat., Museum of Modern Art, New York. New York, 2023, pp. 85, 136, 170, colorpl. 44 and ill. p. 82 (color, detail). \n \nLaura Neufeld in Samantha Friedman. Georgia O'Keeffe: To See Takes Time. Exh. cat., Museum of Modern Art, New York. New York, 2023, pp. 33–34.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"credit line","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026687"}],"content":"Purchase, Mr. and Mrs. Milton Petrie Gift, 1981","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Materials description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/materials_description"}],"content":"Watercolor on paper","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_la